# ShellCheck resolves the path in a '# shellcheck source=' directive relative
# to the working directory, not the file being checked. Every directive in
# this repo is written relative to the directory the script lives in, so
# without SCRIPTDIR the install/ scripts fail to resolve install/lib/common.sh
# (SC1091) unless shellcheck happens to be run from the repo root.
#
# SCRIPTDIR makes those paths resolve against each script's own directory, so
# the same command works no matter where it is invoked from.
source-path=SCRIPTDIR
